    "tree_id": "34b84a8ac453ebf921cdf0bf8512554cf3338740",
    "message": "Raster gate: slug the artifact label so composed families can keep their receipts (#221)\n\nAn artifact name may not contain a colon, and composed-treatment family ids\nare full of them. Six of twenty-four family jobs in run 33574304514 rendered\ncorrectly and then failed at artifact upload for that reason alone, which\nreads as a failed verdict when nothing about the packet failed \u2014 and a failed\njob cannot honestly carry a RASTER_PASS.\n\nGitHub Actions expressions have no replace(), so the label is computed in a\nstep and passed through the environment rather than interpolated into shell\nsource. The family id is untouched; only the artifact label is slugged.\n\nOne file, 14 insertions, 1 deletion. No packet file, ledger, queue, receipt,\napplication code, migration or other workflow; permissions unchanged at\ncontents: read; the gate still requires a hash-bound RASTER_PASS.",
    "timestamp": "2026-09-02T00:55:07Z",
